1
00:02:04,050 --> 00:02:06,900
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:15,020
Tell your soldiers to retreat.

3
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:39,660
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

4
00:02:45,380 --> 00:02:48,920
I didn't expect you to be here this
soon, Osman.

5
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:51,120
It's obvious.

6
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:55,140
If you knew I'd come, you wouldn't have
done what you did.

7
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,940
I have an offer for you, Osman.

8
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:00,380
Osman!

9
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:04,780
I'll set your brother and uncle free...

10
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:09,060
... and in return you'll throw away that
torch.

11
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:36,240
So, after all, you are okay with dying
with me, Osman!

12
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,920
How about you?

13
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:41,660
Are you okay with dying with me along with
this dog of yours?

14
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:43,420
Tell me!

15
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:46,720
Let's do it like this.

16
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:49,980
Let's do it step by step.

17
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:51,600
First throw that...

18
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:53,240
Osman!

19
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,620
Throw that torch!

20
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:02,620
Do what I said!

21
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,840
Set my uncle and brother free.

22
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:24,340
Set them free.

23
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:31,060
Set them free!

24
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:42,680
No, Nikola!

25
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:44,440
Don't let them go!

26
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:46,440
We shall die all together!

27
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:48,180
Flatyos...

28
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,180
Dumrul.

29
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,320
Ayaz.

30
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:31,840
May you set my uncle and brother free.

31
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,400
Now...

32
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:08,940
Take your soldiers along with Flatyos and
retreat.

33
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,540
Come on!

34
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:35,120
How are you going to escape here, Osman?

35
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:41,720
By swinging my arms and hands!

36
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:10,780
Kill him!

37
00:09:59,380 --> 00:10:01,380
Let's go!

38
00:10:39,060 --> 00:10:40,240
Osman!

39
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,520
Where is Osman?

40
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,620
This isn't the flying fire.

41
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:58,380
This isn't the flying fire!

42
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:01,680
He deceived us! It's not the the flying
fire!

43
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:03,440
Soldier!

44
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:05,440
Osman!

45
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:09,260
Come and confront me!

46
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,040
Osman!

47
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:15,840
Mount your horses!

48
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,160
Mount your horses!

49
00:11:49,380 --> 00:11:50,740
Osman!

50
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,200
Ayaz and Dumrul.

51
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:04,880
May you divert the army of dogs!

52
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:06,740
As you order, my Bey.

53
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:09,240
Come on!

54
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,380
Faster!

55
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,700
Don't worry, uncle.

56
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:49,160
We'll make them pay for everything.

57
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:56,340
I neither forgot about the dagger stabbed
at the back of my brother, Gündüz...

58
00:14:57,580 --> 00:15:01,100
... nor the one stabbed at your hand.

59
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:04,480
I will make every single one of them pay!

60
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,600
Every single one of them!

61
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:10,220
May you live long, my nephew.

62
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,200
May you live long.

63
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:16,620
You saved us from that dog.

64
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,580
You came...

65
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:19,460
I came!

66
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,400
I came, uncle!

67
00:15:25,780 --> 00:15:27,800
I had no choice.

68
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:30,640
I couldn't leave you at the hand of that
dog!

69
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,740
I couldn't trust the warrant of Yalvak
Arslan.

70
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:40,960
Just like I couldn't trust the mercy of
Nikola.

71
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:50,940
But how about you?

72
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,440
Tell me, uncle.

73
00:15:54,640 --> 00:15:55,700
Brother.

74
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,160
You will keep trusting them.

75
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:03,700
You will keep believing in the lies of
that enemy, uncle!

76
00:16:07,680 --> 00:16:08,800
Brother!

77
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:11,060
Do you know why?

78
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:15,600
Instead of my factual words...

79
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:22,280
... you prefer the lies spilled from the
mouth of our enemies!

80
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,100
All must do what's best for them!

81
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:38,700
Until...

82
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:40,920
... we don't have any enemies to fight!

83
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,740
Are you bragging, Osman?

84
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:50,790
You say all must do what's best for them.

85
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,800
Is this what's best for you?

86
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:57,060
I still haven't started doing what's
best for me.

87
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:01,880
Uncle!

88
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:03,960
Brother!

89
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:06,359
I'm just trying to warn you.

90
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:12,720
May you go to the Tent now.

91
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:15,380
Ayaz and Dumrul will escort you.

92
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,740
I have things to do.

93
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:43,220
It might be a trap! Be careful!

94
00:18:05,580 --> 00:18:06,900
Charge!

95
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:08,500
Catch them!

96
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,720
I don't want to die.

97
00:18:42,440 --> 00:18:43,780
Don't worry.

98
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:46,140
Flatyos is merciful.

99
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,480
I will save you.

100
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:01,820
I saved you from the wrath of living a
dishonorable life.

101
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:04,300
Because you can't resist that feeling.

102
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:10,160
Osman!

103
00:19:25,780 --> 00:19:26,820
You!

104
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:29,780
I didn't see you before.

105
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:16,080
There will be chaos when the flying fire
explodes.

106
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:18,260
Then you'll sneak into the castle.

107
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,500
The siege of Kulacahisar has started.

108
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:22,580
When I go to that castle again...

109
00:20:22,850 --> 00:20:25,200
...instead of fighting, I will take it
this time.

110
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:28,860
The siege of Kulacahisar has started.

111
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:33,260
We should hurry up, brother.

112
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,960
We still have a lot to do.

113
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:36,060
Let's go.

114
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:06,780
Commander Flatyos!

115
00:21:08,980 --> 00:21:10,460
What's the result?

116
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:32,420
We lost their track at a narrow pass,
Nikola.

117
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:35,860
You lost their track.

118
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:39,460
Am I right?

119
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:44,180
How did that happen?

120
00:21:44,980 --> 00:21:46,460
They trapped us.

121
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:48,440
My soldiers died, Nikola.

122
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:50,300
You got trapped.

123
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:54,060
And you got my soldiers killed, Flatyos!

124
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:01,820
This is my castle!

125
00:22:02,260 --> 00:22:03,900
They are my soldiers!

126
00:22:04,660 --> 00:22:05,720
Mine!

127
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:09,820
Osman killed my soldiers, Flatyos!

128
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,040
My soldiers!

129
00:22:14,040 --> 00:22:16,280
Perhaps you will kill me now, Nikola.

130
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:41,840
What are you doing, Nikola?

131
00:22:41,880 --> 00:22:43,760
I'm killing you, Flatyos!

132
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:57,100
You are no longer a commander of Rome.

133
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:05,320
You are dead now.

134
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:18,400
From now on, you are nothing.

135
00:23:30,160 --> 00:23:32,600
You are not even a soldier, Flatyos.

136
00:24:33,040 --> 00:24:36,020
Osman Bey, we received news about Geyhatu.

137
00:24:37,300 --> 00:24:41,980
Geyhatu knows that he will deflate
Kulacahisar sooner or later.

138
00:24:42,900 --> 00:24:46,360
So he is going to organize a carnival at
the Tent of Yalvak Arslan.

139
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:51,020
And they are going to invite you and make
you break the ice with Nikola.

140
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:53,480
It's fine.

141
00:24:54,900 --> 00:24:56,720
Let them organize their carnival.

142
00:24:57,260 --> 00:25:00,820
Dündar, Savcı, and Gündüz Bey are also
invited.

143
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:08,900
Geyhatu wants you to obey him.

144
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:13,680
Geyhatu strugless to learn the fact that
Turks never obey.

145
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:16,800
He will learn eventually, Osman Bey.

146
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:19,020
He will.

147
00:25:19,900 --> 00:25:21,180
He will.

148
00:25:53,500 --> 00:25:55,340
I won't allow this.

149
00:25:55,920 --> 00:25:58,860
I'm not going to let you die before you
save your own honor!

150
00:25:59,820 --> 00:26:03,860
Flatyos, if you ever try to commit
suicide...

151
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:09,980
... no clergymen, priest, or pastor will
bury you with religious rituals!

152
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:11,620
I promise you that!

153
00:27:30,820 --> 00:27:32,980
I hope everything is okay, Davut brother.

154
00:27:33,420 --> 00:27:35,600
What could happen to Dündar and Savcı Bey?

155
00:27:37,300 --> 00:27:38,880
What about them?

156
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:50,080
They look like they came from Kulacahisar
empty handed.

157
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:54,760
They should be grateful that they came
back.

158
00:28:44,320 --> 00:28:45,900
I'm going to suggest that...

159
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:49,560
... nothing have happened there but...

160
00:28:52,100 --> 00:28:54,400
... Osman and his Alps know about
everything.

161
00:28:56,580 --> 00:28:57,720
Neither Osman...

162
00:28:59,440 --> 00:29:01,660
... nor his Alps will say anything,
nephew.

163
00:29:02,340 --> 00:29:07,580
However, I'm just thinking how we will
look at Osman's face ever again.

164
00:29:08,320 --> 00:29:12,400
They say brothers ought to help each other
no matter what happens, uncle.

165
00:29:14,260 --> 00:29:17,140
Perhaps, someday I will save him from a
trouble too.

166
00:29:17,860 --> 00:29:20,560
After that time, debts we'll be paid.

167
00:29:21,300 --> 00:29:22,980
And we will be even.

168
00:29:23,340 --> 00:29:25,780
Debts may be doubled, Savcı Bey.

169
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:30,100
With Allah's permission, we'll pay them
all one day.

170
00:29:36,100 --> 00:29:38,280
Osman saved you once again.

171
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:40,940
Who knows where he is right now.

172
00:29:44,120 --> 00:29:48,340
How can I betray him while he tries so
much for his Tent?

173
00:29:55,540 --> 00:29:57,580
Oh, Karayel.

174
00:30:00,960 --> 00:30:02,620
Can you see?

175
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:05,820
Can you see?

176
00:30:07,040 --> 00:30:09,900
Even Geyhatu understands that I'll take
Kulacahisar.

177
00:30:12,940 --> 00:30:15,780
However, my uncle and brother did not.

178
00:30:17,820 --> 00:30:21,980
Perhaps, Geyhatu also knows that when I
take Kulacahisar...

179
00:30:22,800 --> 00:30:25,300
...no one will dare to stand against me.

180
00:30:26,720 --> 00:30:28,900
However...

181
00:30:29,380 --> 00:30:31,840
... my uncle and brother still don't
get it.

182
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:36,500
But, eventually they will learn...

183
00:30:36,500 --> 00:30:38,500
... see it...

184
00:30:38,500 --> 00:30:40,500
... and understand it.

185
00:31:00,480 --> 00:31:03,820
And Geyhatu will understand that threats
don't work against me!

186
00:31:07,180 --> 00:31:09,420
May he do his best!

187
00:31:48,940 --> 00:31:50,940
May it be easy, Hatuns.

188
00:31:50,940 --> 00:31:52,560
Thank you.

189
00:31:52,560 --> 00:31:55,500
I'd like to help you if that's okay.

190
00:31:55,860 --> 00:31:57,680
Of course, Targun Hatun!

191
00:32:00,040 --> 00:32:02,640
You've become one of us recently.

192
00:32:05,720 --> 00:32:09,920
Perhaps, someday you will become a bride
of Kayıs.

193
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:12,620
Inshallah.

194
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:22,880
A bride of Kayıs?

195
00:32:23,640 --> 00:32:27,060
Is there even a Kayıbeyi who is not
married?

196
00:32:29,540 --> 00:32:32,760
Does he have to be a Bey?

197
00:32:34,120 --> 00:32:36,120
A Bey's daughter must marry a Bey.

198
00:32:40,460 --> 00:32:44,540
There is no Kayıbeyi who is not married.

199
00:32:44,920 --> 00:32:49,140
But there is a Bey who wants to have a
child.

200
00:32:56,120 --> 00:32:57,760
I hope it's for good.

201
00:32:59,440 --> 00:33:02,000
Are you trying to find a Bey for Targun
now?

202
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:20,960
It’s hard to be a Hatun in Kayı, daughter.

203
00:33:21,240 --> 00:33:25,600
I was hard before. It’s harder now.

204
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:31,440
Our ancestors had
ruled insignificant lands.

205
00:33:32,320 --> 00:33:37,160
Back then, even Hatuns
like Hazal could marry…

206
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:41,400
… stupid Beys and become Hatun of Beys.

207
00:33:45,920 --> 00:33:49,400
But now, things are different.

208
00:33:57,840 --> 00:34:00,480
Kayıs are talking about becoming a state.

209
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:04,240
Being the Hatun of a Kayı Bey…

210
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:07,000
... means being the Hatun of the state.

211
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:12,520
For example, my Osman married Bala Hatun.

212
00:34:12,520 --> 00:34:15,320
.. who was raised by Sheikh Edebali.

213
00:34:21,080 --> 00:34:25,920
A Hatun worthy of ruling the world.

214
00:34:37,320 --> 00:34:43,159
What I mean is, if you want
to be a Kayı Hatun…

215
00:34:43,159 --> 00:34:49,000
… or bring a child to the Kayıs…

216
00:34:50,080 --> 00:34:52,880
… try to be a Bala.

217
00:35:36,360 --> 00:35:39,840
Excuse me. I have things to do.

218
00:35:39,840 --> 00:35:42,320
Of course, daughter. Go, and work!

219
00:36:25,360 --> 00:36:27,360
What happened to you, Bey?

220
00:36:33,840 --> 00:36:37,520
Stop and tell me what happened!

221
00:36:41,160 --> 00:36:44,720
Come on. Tell me.

222
00:36:49,160 --> 00:36:55,480
Osman. He was always mad like this.

223
00:36:55,480 --> 00:37:00,760
He was always bold. He was brave.

224
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:06,720
But he wouldn’t think
about the consequences.

225
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:14,560
I always thought he would die in a battle

226
00:37:16,720 --> 00:37:19,320
before he got this old.

227
00:37:22,680 --> 00:37:32,920
But he’s braver, bolder,
more consistent by day!

228
00:37:36,320 --> 00:37:42,560
This won’t be easy, Hatun.

229
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:57,320
Such a man won’t show
mercy for his cause, right?

230
00:37:59,600 --> 00:38:04,520
You know the tradition.
Osman is the youngest of you.

231
00:38:07,280 --> 00:38:11,840
It’s normal that he’s trying harder
to show that he’s in control.

232
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:20,800
But since our Bey chose you as
the Head Alp, you’re his obstacle.

233
00:38:27,200 --> 00:38:29,200
What do you mean, Hatun?

234
00:38:31,680 --> 00:38:36,640
To be the Kayı’s Bey,
Osman will try to kill you.

235
00:38:43,880 --> 00:38:46,640
What are you saying about
my brother, Hatun?

236
00:38:46,640 --> 00:38:50,040
Your brother won’t do anything
outside the traditions, righT?

237
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:57,480
But if the traditions allow Osman
to take your head, Osman will take it!

238
00:38:59,440 --> 00:39:02,640
What I’m saying is,
before Osman takes your head-

239
00:39:02,640 --> 00:39:04,120
Enough!

240
00:39:06,160 --> 00:39:07,320
Enough!

241
00:39:10,240 --> 00:39:12,000
I’ll ignore what you’ve said.

242
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:14,000
You have to do it, Savcı Bey.

243
00:39:15,080 --> 00:39:19,200
That fire will jump either
on my or Bala’s tent.

244
00:39:27,440 --> 00:39:33,440
You decide whose heart will burn.

245
00:39:39,160 --> 00:39:42,120
I will not shed my brother’s blood!

246
00:39:43,360 --> 00:39:45,760
States are found on blood.

247
00:40:09,960 --> 00:40:12,280
Cerkutay.

248
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:34,640
Cerkutay…

249
00:40:54,120 --> 00:41:00,440
Now tell me. Who did you try
to trick my Osman with?

250
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:06,520
Who let the dogs out? Tell me.

251
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:24,000
I’ll cut you to pieces, Cerkutay.

252
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:29,040
I’ll feed the dogs with your flesh.

253
00:41:29,560 --> 00:41:37,200
So, Cerkutay, tell me
who you work for.

254
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:43,280
Don’t play with me, Cerkutay.

255
00:41:44,440 --> 00:41:47,200
This has been going
on for too long.

256
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:54,280
Let’s not waste any more time then.

257
00:41:56,880 --> 00:41:59,120
Let’s cut it short.

258
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:07,040
Or should I cut your throat?

259
00:42:07,480 --> 00:42:13,600
I should start with your ears.
First one, then the other.

260
00:42:15,680 --> 00:42:21,680
You’ll still talk, but you
won’t hear a thing you say!

261
00:42:23,960 --> 00:42:26,720
Let’s start with this ear.

262
00:42:28,520 --> 00:42:30,880
Wait!

263
00:42:33,120 --> 00:42:35,080
Yavlak Arslan!

264
00:42:49,200 --> 00:42:50,840
Yavlak Arslan.

265
00:43:04,440 --> 00:43:14,800
Yavlak Arslan!

266
00:43:23,640 --> 00:43:27,680
What is it Targun Hatun?
Where are you going?

267
00:43:28,480 --> 00:43:32,840
I feel tired.
I’ll rest in my tent.

268
00:43:41,160 --> 00:43:45,720
She’s up to something.
She thinks no one will notice.

269
00:44:07,560 --> 00:44:11,880
Gonca.
Find out where she’s going.

270
00:44:11,880 --> 00:44:15,920
I’ll keep my eyes on her.
Don’t worry.

271
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:32,200
- My Bey!
- Talk.

272
00:44:32,200 --> 00:44:33,680
Cerkutay talked.

273
00:44:36,360 --> 00:44:39,360
Let’s see who was
playing tricks on us.

274
00:44:39,360 --> 00:44:43,600
Yavlak Arslan. He’s also the one
who had been working with Möngke.

275
00:44:44,680 --> 00:44:46,600
Let no one in
the Tent hear about this.

276
00:44:46,600 --> 00:44:48,200
As you order, my Bey.

277
00:44:49,440 --> 00:44:52,320
I’ll make them pay for this.

278
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:11,880
Who do you think will
replace Flatyos?

279
00:45:12,280 --> 00:45:14,480
Whoever replaces him will be better.

280
00:45:23,120 --> 00:45:27,960
Who are you to talk about
commander Flatyos? Pity.

281
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:30,320
Where are my manners?

282
00:45:31,120 --> 00:45:33,080
Let’s go.

283
00:46:11,360 --> 00:46:13,120
This road leads to the castle.

284
00:46:13,760 --> 00:46:17,760
What are you up to,
Targun Hatun?

285
00:46:46,520 --> 00:46:48,760
I’m here for the Landlord.

286
00:46:49,760 --> 00:46:53,080
Brother, isn’t that Targun Hatun?

287
00:46:53,080 --> 00:46:54,600
Her very self!

288
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:18,880
What is she doing here?

289
00:47:23,920 --> 00:47:26,040
Let’s go, brother.

290
00:47:48,560 --> 00:47:53,800
What are you doing here?
Why arent you in the Tent?

291
00:47:53,800 --> 00:47:55,970
I brought you the information
you asked for.

292
00:47:55,970 --> 00:47:57,680
Let my father our and I’ll leave.

293
00:47:57,680 --> 00:48:01,680
Osman attacked me twice and
I was aware of only one!

294
00:48:01,680 --> 00:48:03,960
But you did what I asked, is that it?

295
00:48:03,960 --> 00:48:05,240
It wasn’t my fault!

296
00:48:05,240 --> 00:48:09,840
Tergun! Osman
is more powerful than before!

297
00:48:09,840 --> 00:48:13,560
Please tell me how your job is done!

298
00:48:19,360 --> 00:48:21,640
I don’t want to do it anymore.

299
00:48:24,880 --> 00:48:26,360
Is that so?

300
00:48:27,360 --> 00:48:31,520
And I don’t want to listen
to your nonsense, Tergun.

301
00:48:33,720 --> 00:48:35,960
I don’t like nonsense.

302
00:48:36,400 --> 00:48:41,360
Show me my father, Nikola.
I must be sure that he’s alive.

303
00:48:42,360 --> 00:48:44,600
Don’t you trust me?

304
00:48:48,000 --> 00:48:52,760
Let me show you your father.

305
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:01,000
Why don’t you come?!

306
00:49:02,600 --> 00:49:04,560
Bring her.

307
00:49:31,440 --> 00:49:34,960
What is it, my Bala?
Did something happen?

308
00:49:34,960 --> 00:49:37,360
Targun Hatun left the tent, my Bey.

309
00:49:37,360 --> 00:49:44,000
I sent Gonca after her.
She said saw her going to Kulacahisar.

310
00:49:48,160 --> 00:49:52,920
So, she went to Kulacahisar.

311
00:49:58,600 --> 00:50:03,600
Thank you, my Bala.
I’ll deal with the rest.

312
00:50:05,680 --> 00:50:08,080
Why would she go to that castle?

313
00:50:08,080 --> 00:50:10,120
Don’t worry, Bala.

314
00:50:10,120 --> 00:50:14,800
After I conquer that castle,
every malice inside will be gone!

315
00:50:14,800 --> 00:50:17,080
Don’t worry, my Bala.

316
00:50:18,040 --> 00:50:19,760
Then?

317
00:50:21,520 --> 00:50:26,080
You’ll be a Bey. Right, Osman?

318
00:50:43,200 --> 00:50:49,160
Of course, I’ll be a Bey.
Does that make you sad, my Bala?

319
00:50:53,600 --> 00:50:56,400
You need an heir, Osman.

320
00:50:57,360 --> 00:51:00,880
You need a Hatun who
will give you an heir.

321
00:51:11,360 --> 00:51:14,160
It is now time, Osman Bey.

322
00:51:14,840 --> 00:51:20,240
For the future of Kayı,
you need to find a new Hatun.

323
00:51:28,120 --> 00:51:30,480
What are you saying, my Bala?

324
00:51:32,320 --> 00:51:38,280
If you don’t do it
so I’m not sad…

325
00:51:38,280 --> 00:51:40,840
… I’ll find you that Hatun.

326
00:51:55,640 --> 00:52:00,480
Bala!

327
00:52:52,800 --> 00:52:55,120
Father!

328
00:52:56,520 --> 00:52:57,840
Daughter!

329
00:52:58,640 --> 00:53:00,400
Open the door!

330
00:53:00,400 --> 00:53:02,880
- My daughter. - Father!

331
00:53:03,280 --> 00:53:05,560
Open, I said!

332
00:53:06,280 --> 00:53:08,760
Open it.

333
00:53:11,600 --> 00:53:14,480
Come on! Move!

334
00:53:15,560 --> 00:53:20,360
- Father! - My daughter!

335
00:53:20,360 --> 00:53:25,160
Father! Are you okay?

336
00:53:31,280 --> 00:53:33,400
What did you do to my father?

337
00:53:33,640 --> 00:53:38,800
I agree. Should I tell
the guards to be more careful?

338
00:53:52,920 --> 00:53:58,360
You’re alive. Don’t
think about me, daughter.

339
00:53:59,960 --> 00:54:02,640
They want me to betray the Turks, father.

340
00:54:02,640 --> 00:54:05,440
Don’t do it, daughter!

341
00:54:05,440 --> 00:54:10,040
Don’t throw yourself
in the fire to save me.

342
00:54:11,680 --> 00:54:17,640
They are our brothers!
These dogs are nothing to us!

343
00:54:17,640 --> 00:54:22,320
But she has to hold on, right Targun?

344
00:54:24,040 --> 00:54:26,440
Or her father will die.

345
00:54:28,320 --> 00:54:34,360
Let me put it this way, if necessary,
she’ll even sleep with Osman.

346
00:54:35,360 --> 00:54:39,120
Nikola! I will skin you, Nikola!

347
00:54:39,840 --> 00:54:45,520
If I let you live, there
might be a chance. Maybe.

348
00:54:56,360 --> 00:55:00,840
Targun Hatun.
Before there are no more Turks…

349
00:55:00,840 --> 00:55:03,480
… your job won’t be over.

350
00:55:03,800 --> 00:55:08,600
Otherwise, your father dies.

351
00:55:10,720 --> 00:55:14,640
If it’s not enough, you’ll die.

352
00:55:16,040 --> 00:55:21,040
Or I could tell Osman I have a spy.

353
00:55:21,920 --> 00:55:26,160
Then either Osman kills you…

354
00:55:34,400 --> 00:55:37,640
Your choice.

355
00:55:39,920 --> 00:55:42,160
You’ll live, father!

356
00:55:42,160 --> 00:55:45,640
You’ll get out of here
and take our revenge!

357
00:55:45,640 --> 00:55:49,120
When that day comes, I’ll be there.

358
00:55:49,120 --> 00:55:52,680
- I promise.
- Let me go!

359
00:55:52,680 --> 00:55:54,880
I promise! I will take our revenge!

360
00:55:54,880 --> 00:56:00,840
- Father!
- I promise!

361
00:56:28,280 --> 00:56:32,360
You said you’d repair my sword.
Why did you put it there?

362
00:56:33,120 --> 00:56:37,280
Osman Bey’s orders.
I’ll forge new swords.

363
00:56:37,280 --> 00:56:39,400
Your’s might wait for a little.

364
00:56:39,400 --> 00:56:41,800
Who told you mine could wait?

365
00:56:41,800 --> 00:56:46,320
Why shouldn’t it? Kayı
Beys’ Hatuns will relax a little.

366
00:56:46,320 --> 00:56:52,120
They shouldn’t worry. I promised
Selcan Hatun to leave them alone.

367
00:56:52,120 --> 00:56:53,840
Now that’s good news.

368
00:56:55,800 --> 00:56:58,760
You repair my sword
and I’ll forge that steel.

369
00:56:58,760 --> 00:57:03,320
How could a woman forge steel?

370
00:57:06,920 --> 00:57:09,920
Give me that and everyone will see.

371
00:57:36,680 --> 00:57:39,760
Where are you going, Targun Hatun?

372
00:57:53,480 --> 00:57:57,920
Osman Bey! I’m…

373
00:58:00,360 --> 00:58:01,840
I was returning to the Tent.

374
00:58:01,840 --> 00:58:03,440
I see.

375
00:58:03,880 --> 00:58:11,440
I know where you’re going.
Where are you returning from?

376
00:58:18,240 --> 00:58:20,560
What are you up to?

377
00:58:20,960 --> 00:58:24,320
You’re one of those who
will be settled up with!

378
00:59:07,680 --> 00:59:10,840
Allah is one!

379
00:59:10,840 --> 00:59:13,360
Allah is great!

380
00:59:13,360 --> 00:59:16,080
Allah is one!

381
00:59:16,080 --> 00:59:18,400
Allah is great!

382
00:59:28,120 --> 00:59:30,680
People!

383
00:59:34,480 --> 00:59:42,040
From now on, the days of
‘you can’t do it’ are over.

384
00:59:44,240 --> 00:59:50,280
This is the Tent of Osman bey who’ll be
taking Kulacahisar with a handful of Alps.

385
00:59:50,280 --> 00:59:53,680
Here, everyone will do
what others call impossible!

386
01:00:22,320 --> 01:00:24,600
Good work, master.

387
01:00:25,320 --> 01:00:27,880
It looks like a
real sword now.

388
01:00:35,960 --> 01:00:39,480
Sisters! When it’s about battle…

389
01:00:39,480 --> 01:00:43,040
… you don’t have to wait
for your Beys’ permissions.

390
01:00:44,160 --> 01:00:49,560
When Osman Bey gives the orders,
you’ll take your swords and follow me!

391
01:00:51,160 --> 01:00:54,240
But you need to be trained.

392
01:01:02,840 --> 01:01:08,080
Good luck, master. Thank you.

393
01:01:24,360 --> 01:01:28,440
May my Allah cure her
as soon as possible.

394
01:01:29,400 --> 01:01:33,720
Let’s mind our own
businesses. Let’s go!

395
01:01:43,560 --> 01:01:46,840
What are you up to with Nikola?

396
01:01:47,280 --> 01:01:49,800
Tell me one by one!

397
01:01:51,240 --> 01:01:52,920
I will tell you.

398
01:02:17,040 --> 01:02:19,600
You want to die fighting!

399
01:02:20,080 --> 01:02:21,960
I will die one day.

400
01:02:21,960 --> 01:02:27,600
In my funeral, they’ll call me
‘The woman who killed Osman Bey’!

401
01:02:27,600 --> 01:02:32,840
Of course. Everyone
in your funeral will hear this.

402
01:02:36,640 --> 01:02:39,000
But they’ll hear it from me.

403
01:02:40,720 --> 01:02:42,240
We’ll see.

404
01:03:30,920 --> 01:03:35,320
I know you well.
You don’t attack the unarmed.

405
01:03:53,400 --> 01:03:55,480
Stop this nonsense!

406
01:03:56,080 --> 01:03:58,280
What are you up to with Nikola?

407
01:04:04,680 --> 01:04:06,560
My father…

408
01:04:14,560 --> 01:04:20,000
Don’t be afraid.
You’re safe.

409
01:04:33,000 --> 01:04:35,040
I’ll tell you.

410
01:04:43,240 --> 01:04:45,400
They wanted to meet me.

411
01:04:45,600 --> 01:04:48,240
They had captured my men.

412
01:04:50,400 --> 01:04:52,600
Kurgun!

413
01:04:57,600 --> 01:05:02,000
Güneş! What did they do to you?

414
01:05:03,040 --> 01:05:06,840
How could you do this?
Let them go!

415
01:05:23,440 --> 01:05:24,880
Come and get it.

416
01:05:24,880 --> 01:05:27,480
I’ll rip you apart and
take that key!

417
01:05:34,000 --> 01:05:36,600
I can’t wait, Targun.

418
01:05:42,760 --> 01:05:44,720
Where is my father?

419
01:05:45,360 --> 01:05:51,160
If you want to see your father,
you have to accept Nikola’s offer.

420
01:05:51,160 --> 01:05:56,680
No one threatens us Kuman Turks!

421
01:05:56,680 --> 01:05:59,800
Where is my father, I said!

422
01:06:00,160 --> 01:06:06,560
Targun. If you want to see your
father, you have to deserve it.

423
01:06:06,560 --> 01:06:08,560
Die, degenerate!

424
01:06:19,280 --> 01:06:21,400
You’re as good as Nikola mentioned.

425
01:06:21,400 --> 01:06:23,600
But not that much.

426
01:06:56,560 --> 01:06:58,360
Father!

427
01:07:23,760 --> 01:07:26,200
I want something from you.

428
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:30,760
You’ll give me Osman, Targun.

429
01:07:33,040 --> 01:07:40,480
I’ll hear and feel every step
he takes and every move he makes…

430
01:07:40,480 --> 01:07:42,680
… with you.

431
01:07:47,520 --> 01:07:50,640
When you give me what I want…

432
01:07:50,640 --> 01:07:55,440
… I’ll give you your father and your men.

433
01:08:00,040 --> 01:08:03,360
Maybe more.

434
01:08:06,960 --> 01:08:11,840
I like rewards.

435
01:08:13,760 --> 01:08:18,680
By the way, these poor
guys didn’t eat anything yet.

436
01:08:18,680 --> 01:08:23,160
If you accept it,
they’ll eat something.

437
01:08:23,160 --> 01:08:25,560
They are about to starve.

438
01:08:36,600 --> 01:08:38,200
Your choice.

439
01:08:40,960 --> 01:08:44,000
You’ll give me Osman, Targun.

440
01:08:46,399 --> 01:08:48,720
What will you do with me?

441
01:08:50,240 --> 01:08:53,240
So, Nikola wanted
me from you.

442
01:08:56,840 --> 01:08:59,680
Let’s give him what he wants.

443
01:09:15,319 --> 01:09:18,240
We heard that Osman Bey
was looking for a new Hatun.

444
01:09:18,240 --> 01:09:19,960
What are you talking about, Hatun?

445
01:09:19,960 --> 01:09:22,000
Since you can’t get pregnant.

446
01:09:22,000 --> 01:09:23,640
Osman will hear about it.

447
01:09:23,640 --> 01:09:26,000
He’ll be embarrassed because of me.

448
01:09:26,000 --> 01:09:29,640
Don’t give up just yet.
It has to have a cure.

449
01:09:29,640 --> 01:09:34,439
Doesn’t matter, Gonca.
I think about Osman.

450
01:09:35,359 --> 01:09:40,600
He has dreams. I don’t want those
dreams to be crushed because of me.

451
01:09:40,600 --> 01:09:43,359
What can you do other than
look for solutions?

452
01:09:43,359 --> 01:09:48,200
I’d sacrifice myself for Osman, Gonca!

453
01:09:48,200 --> 01:09:53,319
You need a Hatun who
will give you an heir Osman.

454
01:09:58,320 --> 01:10:00,400
What are you saying, Bala?

455
01:10:02,680 --> 01:10:09,880
If you don’t, I’ll find
you that Hatun!

456
01:10:13,600 --> 01:10:17,800
Osman is the hope
of every Turk out there.

457
01:10:17,800 --> 01:10:23,760
If it will keep that hope alive, I’ll
watch my Osman marry another Hatun.

458
01:10:45,200 --> 01:10:47,280
I wonder what happened now.

459
01:10:54,840 --> 01:10:58,960
Bala? What happened?

460
01:11:00,880 --> 01:11:03,720
Tell me, Bala.

461
01:11:05,080 --> 01:11:07,880
We said we’d hide
nothing from each other.

462
01:11:13,320 --> 01:11:15,160
I…

463
01:11:16,720 --> 01:11:19,160
I told Osman Bey to…

464
01:11:20,400 --> 01:11:23,320
… find himself another Hatun.

465
01:11:30,800 --> 01:11:33,000
What did Osman Bey say?

466
01:11:34,280 --> 01:11:36,240
He didn’t want to accept it.

467
01:11:36,960 --> 01:11:39,000
He didn’t accept it, Bala!

468
01:11:39,680 --> 01:11:41,480
Don’t worry.

469
01:11:41,480 --> 01:11:46,080
Gonca, as you know
he has to accept it.

470
01:11:47,120 --> 01:11:49,000
And he will.

471
01:11:53,520 --> 01:11:56,360
But I don’t want it.

472
01:11:57,200 --> 01:11:58,760
Bala!

473
01:12:05,840 --> 01:12:11,000
Poor little one. What did you do wrong?

474
01:12:11,000 --> 01:12:13,720
One part of you will always be missing.

475
01:12:13,720 --> 01:12:18,920
You’ll always wonder
if someone is talking about you.

476
01:12:26,560 --> 01:12:30,800
Bala? What happened?

477
01:12:30,800 --> 01:12:36,320
Come, sit. What made you sad?

478
01:12:38,640 --> 01:12:43,040
Neither of us did anything wrong.

479
01:12:45,640 --> 01:12:52,400
This is how the creator wanted.
We have to be patient, Selcan mother.

480
01:12:52,760 --> 01:12:55,880
My Bala. My beautiful daughter.

481
01:12:58,880 --> 01:13:02,400
- Mother!
- Your mother would die for you.

482
01:13:03,080 --> 01:13:06,680
Selcan mother!
I won’t be a mother!

483
01:13:13,240 --> 01:13:15,280
Don’t say that, my Bala.

484
01:14:35,532 --> 01:14:39,302
Do you know what we are looking at, Lena?

485
01:14:40,121 --> 01:14:41,701
What?

486
01:14:44,462 --> 01:14:48,262
The new bride of the Kayı.

487
01:14:51,758 --> 01:14:57,968
You might be right, Hazal Hatun.
Then, Bala's heart will burn.

488
01:14:58,156 --> 01:15:05,846
And your heart will ease. But,
if Osman has a son from that woman...

489
01:15:05,921 --> 01:15:09,921
...what will happen to us?
Think about that, as well.

490
01:15:10,561 --> 01:15:18,031
Mashallah, my girl. You think that
I don't think about that. You are wrong.

491
01:15:18,934 --> 01:15:27,724
Firstly, you should take care of the enemy
that is close. The other is for later.

492
01:16:35,685 --> 01:16:38,075
-Brother.
-Brother.

493
01:16:40,958 --> 01:16:46,178
Geyhatu had sent a word. He wants
you to make peace with Nikola.

494
01:16:48,789 --> 01:16:50,849
What will he do otherwise?

495
01:16:51,749 --> 01:16:57,579
Otherwise, he'll come here with his army,
and destroy the whole place.

496
01:17:06,255 --> 01:17:10,255
We wouldn't want that, brother, right?

497
01:17:10,400 --> 01:17:13,110
Of course not, brother.

498
01:17:17,891 --> 01:17:23,111
What do you think that we should do?

499
01:17:25,492 --> 01:17:32,132
Yavlak Arslan will host both sides.
You will make peace in his presence.

500
01:17:32,971 --> 01:17:37,271
Osman, I say that you
should accept it, brother.

501
01:17:38,591 --> 01:17:45,381
Right, Yavlak Arslan is
the bey of the beys.

502
01:17:46,567 --> 01:17:53,017
Osman, look, we just got
rid of the Mongol trouble.

503
01:17:55,364 --> 01:18:01,174
-Don't.
-Don't worry, brother. Geyhatu won't return here.

504
01:18:02,055 --> 01:18:06,805
Will you accept it?
Will you come together with Nikola?

505
01:18:09,486 --> 01:18:12,796
If Geyhatu wants so.

506
01:18:16,786 --> 01:18:21,666
I didn't think that I could
convince you. Thank you, brother.

507
01:18:22,183 --> 01:18:27,023
-Savcı and my uncle will be happy.
-They should be happy.

508
01:18:27,814 --> 01:18:33,904
-We haven't eaten as a family, for a while.
-Right.

509
01:18:39,977 --> 01:18:45,207
And women are fighting. The tents
should have some peace.

510
01:18:45,257 --> 01:18:49,997
Don't you worry, brother. I'll take care
of that. Good idea.

511
01:19:02,768 --> 01:19:09,498
And in the evening, during dinner,
I'll talk about something important.

512
01:19:11,447 --> 01:19:15,447
All right, brother.
We'll listen to you carefully.

513
01:19:19,283 --> 01:19:21,113
Come on.

514
01:19:32,554 --> 01:19:35,904
The arsenal is behind
that street, brother.

515
01:19:35,904 --> 01:19:38,084
Then it should its gates closed, brother.

516
01:19:38,084 --> 01:19:41,355
It should stay closed until we take
the castle, brother.

517
01:19:52,869 --> 01:19:54,489
You!

518
01:19:56,347 --> 01:19:59,427
-Are you talking to us?
-Yes, I'm talking to you!

519
01:20:05,717 --> 01:20:07,687
Let's hide them.

520
01:20:26,495 --> 01:20:34,025
My bey, Geyhatu made Yavlak Arslan
bey of beys.

521
01:20:34,569 --> 01:20:39,139
Dündar and Savcı Beys are working
with him.

522
01:20:39,357 --> 01:20:43,357
They see the future of the Kayı
in him.

523
01:20:43,632 --> 01:20:48,662
Osman Bey is following his own politics.

524
01:20:49,279 --> 01:20:53,279
He doesn't leave Kulucahisar.

525
01:20:54,192 --> 01:20:59,712
Osman doesn't recognize Yavlak Arslan,
my bey.

526
01:20:59,879 --> 01:21:05,679
Gündüz Bey is with Savcı and
Dündar Beys, mentally...

527
01:21:05,710 --> 01:21:09,710
...but in heart, he is
with Osman Bey.

528
01:21:10,415 --> 01:21:15,145
He is trying to stop his brother
but Osman...

529
01:21:15,512 --> 01:21:19,512
What's happening, Abdurrahman Ghazi?
Is our bey awaken?

530
01:21:25,260 --> 01:21:29,260
My bey wanted me to tell the
situation of the Kayı.

531
01:21:29,730 --> 01:21:33,730
And I'm telling him, maybe
he can hear me.

532
01:21:38,352 --> 01:21:43,032
He can hear. He can hear, surely.

533
01:21:43,108 --> 01:21:47,718
Both his ears and heart
are with us. He hears us.

534
01:21:48,705 --> 01:21:54,585
Brother, you are worried about
how we are? Don't.

535
01:21:56,431 --> 01:22:01,071
We are side by side,
shoulder to shoulder. Thank Allah.

536
01:22:17,261 --> 01:22:19,621
Father...

537
01:22:20,397 --> 01:22:26,057
...tonight, we'll eat together,
as a family.

538
01:22:28,149 --> 01:22:31,679
Just like when you were
with us.

539
01:22:34,200 --> 01:22:37,470
Just like that good days.

540
01:22:45,444 --> 01:22:51,104
Our friends are jealous of our unity,
our enemies are scared.

541
01:22:51,902 --> 01:22:54,942
They can't dare to
sow discontent among us.

542
01:22:55,396 --> 01:22:59,396
We protect your trust well.

543
01:23:13,943 --> 01:23:20,113
Father! The flag that you
put in Söğüt is rising.

544
01:23:21,655 --> 01:23:34,055
Kulucahisar, İnegöl, İznik
and Bursa are waiting.

545
01:23:36,689 --> 01:23:40,689
You brought us from barren land
to here.

546
01:23:41,369 --> 01:23:45,369
We, three brothers...

547
01:23:48,843 --> 01:23:52,843
...will take your flag,
your honorable name...

548
01:23:55,653 --> 01:23:59,153
...from lands to seas.

549
01:24:09,014 --> 01:24:11,944
O' Ghazi's son Ghazi...

550
01:24:13,496 --> 01:24:17,496
...if you hear the voice of
your son Osman...

551
01:24:18,160 --> 01:24:22,160
...know that the flame of holy
war that you started is still alive.

552
01:24:36,175 --> 01:24:39,525
Father.

553
01:25:03,904 --> 01:25:06,654
Father.

554
01:25:33,549 --> 01:25:35,329
Lad.

555
01:25:38,556 --> 01:25:40,896
He heard me.

556
01:25:43,542 --> 01:25:47,542
-He heard me.
-He did? Do you say he heard you?

557
01:25:48,088 --> 01:25:52,088
Mashallah to my bey.
Mashallah.

558
01:25:55,678 --> 01:25:58,618
I told him about İznik...

559
01:25:59,572 --> 01:26:03,872
...Bursa and further...

560
01:26:06,796 --> 01:26:09,396
...even more further...

561
01:26:10,865 --> 01:26:14,865
...I told him about the overseas,
Bamsı Bey.

562
01:26:20,407 --> 01:26:26,877
A tear dropped from his eye.

563
01:26:31,136 --> 01:26:34,376
It was like...

564
01:26:38,730 --> 01:26:42,110
...a power passed
from his hand...

565
01:26:43,076 --> 01:26:45,696
...to my hand, Bamsı Bey.

566
01:26:47,258 --> 01:26:51,828
You say that he felt it?

567
01:26:55,817 --> 01:26:58,597
Mashallah to my bey.

568
01:27:16,524 --> 01:27:19,874
Are we ready, Bamsı Bey?

569
01:27:21,108 --> 01:27:25,108
We are, we are, thank Allah.

570
01:27:25,459 --> 01:27:31,369
-Will we take that castle?
-With Allah's approval, yes.

571
01:27:31,844 --> 01:27:37,034
Then, we should be on its
gates at once.

572
01:27:37,366 --> 01:27:44,646
We should, lad. We should.
I'll personally break that gate.

573
01:28:17,537 --> 01:28:20,857
May Allah bless Gündüz Bey.

574
01:28:22,040 --> 01:28:25,040
We brought us together.

575
01:28:30,905 --> 01:28:36,185
You came to my tent,
you brought joy. Thank you.

576
01:28:38,033 --> 01:28:40,153
Thank you.

577
01:28:40,159 --> 01:28:46,419
Thank you, uncle. But since our father
hasn't recovered yet, we are sorrowful.

578
01:28:46,946 --> 01:28:50,946
But if we support each other...

579
01:28:53,409 --> 01:29:02,339
...if we keep our hearts good,
we can pass these difficult days.

580
01:29:03,398 --> 01:29:07,398
-Isn't that so, brother?
-You are right, brother.

581
01:29:09,381 --> 01:29:14,671
What do we have that we can't share
that we can sit and talk two sentences?

582
01:29:21,671 --> 01:29:25,671
I like that. Thank Allah.

583
01:29:25,861 --> 01:29:28,981
Be like this always.

584
01:29:31,951 --> 01:29:35,951
Come on, then.
With the name of Allah.

585
01:29:35,951 --> 01:29:39,151
With the name of Allah.

586
01:29:52,879 --> 01:29:56,089
With the name of Allah.

587
01:30:04,143 --> 01:30:05,953
Osman.

588
01:30:06,714 --> 01:30:10,494
You said that you had something
important to tell us.

589
01:30:11,397 --> 01:30:14,887
Tell us if it's the time, brother.

590
01:30:27,468 --> 01:30:30,648
Dargun Hatun!

591
01:32:18,889 --> 01:32:25,579
So, Osman obeyed Geyhatu's orders
and accepted peace, is that so? Good.

592
01:32:26,332 --> 01:32:34,262
Good. Send the word to Flatyos. He'll kill
Osman on his way to Yavlak Arslan.

593
01:32:34,262 --> 01:32:36,102
As you command.

594
01:32:49,772 --> 01:32:52,562
You called me, Nikola.

595
01:32:52,581 --> 01:32:59,631
Yes, I did. I'm going to Yavlak Arslan's
tents. You'll have the command here.

596
01:33:00,701 --> 01:33:04,701
What if Osman tries another visit?

597
01:33:05,379 --> 01:33:10,299
That sheep shepherd isn't stupid enough
to dare to face Geyhatu.

598
01:33:11,961 --> 01:33:19,111
Are you sure of that? What if he is that
stupid? What if he comes after you leave?

599
01:33:19,529 --> 01:33:25,649
Helen? Do you mean that you can't
protect the castle?

600
01:33:28,777 --> 01:33:32,777
I want to know if you take
that chance or not.

601
01:33:39,798 --> 01:33:45,628
Let's say that Osman comes to the castle
and takes Kulucahisar...

602
01:33:46,155 --> 01:33:48,785
...what will happen then, Helen?

603
01:33:50,443 --> 01:33:56,113
He'll be declared war on Geyhatu.
What'll happen then?

604
01:33:56,683 --> 01:34:02,103
Geyhatu will smash him and
the Kayıs like little bugs.

605
01:34:03,464 --> 01:34:08,204
And we'll fulfill our goals.

606
01:34:09,018 --> 01:34:15,568
Helen, I like every way
of winning.

607
01:34:17,004 --> 01:34:19,724
You do.

608
01:34:31,466 --> 01:34:34,456
Sit, Dargun Hatun.

609
01:34:50,031 --> 01:34:53,511
I thought a lot about it.

610
01:35:05,259 --> 01:35:09,769
A Kayı bey can't be without
a heir.

611
01:35:25,505 --> 01:35:28,465
Dargun Hatun.

612
01:35:30,770 --> 01:35:34,320
Will be my wife from now on.

613
01:35:49,592 --> 01:35:54,502
And she will give me an heir.

614
01:36:26,296 --> 01:36:30,296
Osman Bey made the best decision.

615
01:36:48,263 --> 01:36:52,653
I want it more than anyone for
Osman Bey to have a child.

616
01:37:08,045 --> 01:37:12,045
Inshallah, they can have a son soon.

617
01:37:16,301 --> 01:37:22,581
And no one will have anything else to say.
-Inshallah, inshallah.

618
01:37:26,335 --> 01:37:28,945
Inshallah.

619
01:37:38,237 --> 01:37:48,437
Selcan Hatun, what were you saying?
How does a bride come to the Kayı?

620
01:37:51,545 --> 01:37:58,805
Aygül. My heart is already on fire,
don't fuel it up.

621
01:38:09,959 --> 01:38:13,179
And I have no word for you, Osman.

622
01:38:17,816 --> 01:38:21,816
Tomorrow, I'll come to Yavlak Arslan's
meeting.

623
01:38:23,494 --> 01:38:28,914
But before that, I and Bala will go to
the place that we met with each other.

624
01:38:43,000 --> 01:38:46,480
We'll meet again.

625
01:38:47,235 --> 01:38:50,725
As you wish, Osman.

626
01:38:52,325 --> 01:38:55,585
As you wish.

627
01:38:57,581 --> 01:39:00,031
Then...

628
01:39:01,041 --> 01:39:04,161
Welcome again, my girl.

629
01:39:06,788 --> 01:39:11,378
May Allah make you happy.

630
01:39:11,832 --> 01:39:16,692
May Allah make you happy.

631
01:39:18,071 --> 01:39:23,191
Inshallah, you'll have
many children.

632
01:39:34,492 --> 01:39:39,262
Come on. Enjoy your meal.

633
01:40:15,096 --> 01:40:19,246
The secret has been revealed.
The secret has been revealed.

634
01:40:20,493 --> 01:40:23,353
The secret of love has been revealed.

635
01:40:24,573 --> 01:40:28,323
The lover's heart is a fire scene.

636
01:40:31,195 --> 01:40:36,235
When love falls in your heart, it destroys
everything.

637
01:40:39,744 --> 01:40:43,454
At that time...

638
01:40:44,559 --> 01:40:47,599
The lover can even pass out.

639
01:40:50,103 --> 01:40:53,823
Lovers, ah lovers.

640
01:40:54,823 --> 01:41:00,533
Only the lovers understands the ones
who lost their lover.

641
01:41:14,154 --> 01:41:17,354
Our Sare mother was infertile.

642
01:41:17,996 --> 01:41:25,396
Hz. Ibrahim didn't complain, but didn't
give up his hope either.

643
01:41:26,988 --> 01:41:32,478
Our Sare mother said:
"Your generation should continue...

644
01:41:33,553 --> 01:41:36,113
but I am infertile...

645
01:41:38,146 --> 01:41:41,476
you should marry a young woman."

646
01:41:45,186 --> 01:41:47,546
That's what she said, little lamb.

647
01:41:47,784 --> 01:41:49,784
That's what she said.

648
01:41:53,080 --> 01:41:58,480
When young woman went in the tent
with Hz. Ibrahim...

649
01:41:59,142 --> 01:42:02,642
Our Sare mother felt strange.

650
01:42:04,497 --> 01:42:06,627
How can she not?

651
01:42:07,474 --> 01:42:09,474
How can she not?

652
01:42:09,597 --> 01:42:13,987
We are coming from a single god,
how can we tolerate duality?

653
01:42:24,099 --> 01:42:28,809
Burning...
Burning...

654
01:42:30,283 --> 01:42:33,553
When the secrets meet...

655
01:42:39,261 --> 01:42:40,611
My Bala.

656
01:42:43,834 --> 01:42:47,044
Am I interrupting our happiness?

657
01:42:50,583 --> 01:42:53,683
It's not you, Osman.

658
01:42:54,990 --> 01:42:57,390
It's a dagger wound.

659
01:42:58,975 --> 01:43:03,345
That wound would heal
sometimes.

660
01:43:04,254 --> 01:43:06,774
But now it won't heal again.

661
01:43:07,772 --> 01:43:09,672
That's all.

662
01:43:10,508 --> 01:43:13,538
That dagger wounded my heart, Bala.

663
01:43:14,751 --> 01:43:19,991
As I see you pale like this,
I get exhausted.

664
01:43:22,186 --> 01:43:23,866
But...

665
01:43:26,690 --> 01:43:28,810
But remember that...

666
01:43:30,146 --> 01:43:35,736
When Our Sare mother give up her hope,
our Lord granted her with a child.

667
01:43:39,858 --> 01:43:42,178
I know Osman.

668
01:43:42,981 --> 01:43:46,481
Hz Ibrahim was about to sacrifice Ismail.

669
01:43:48,421 --> 01:43:50,101
My Bala.

670
01:43:55,401 --> 01:43:57,731
I won't sacrifice you.

671
01:43:58,424 --> 01:44:00,664
I'd die for you.

672
01:44:05,343 --> 01:44:07,573
- Osman.
- Yes?

673
01:44:09,408 --> 01:44:11,988
I know you are going to Kulucahisar.

674
01:44:14,769 --> 01:44:19,919
What I want from you is to take
me there.

675
01:44:23,288 --> 01:44:25,458
Why is that, my Bala?

676
01:44:27,289 --> 01:44:29,239
Why is that?

677
01:44:34,148 --> 01:44:35,658
Do you...

678
01:44:37,257 --> 01:44:40,697
want to be martyr and be free of
your pains?

679
01:44:43,155 --> 01:44:45,905
I become martyr someday in sha Allah,
Osman.

680
01:44:50,493 --> 01:44:53,273
But I want to witness first.

681
01:44:54,370 --> 01:45:00,930
Witness that you become a Bey, you have
sons to carry your Beyship on.

682
01:45:11,413 --> 01:45:13,133
Bala.

683
01:45:13,994 --> 01:45:16,424
Then you should promise me.

684
01:45:16,756 --> 01:45:18,656
What promise?

685
01:45:19,104 --> 01:45:25,084
You are not going to put yourself in
danger in Kulucahisar.

686
01:45:25,954 --> 01:45:29,374
Don't burn my heart.

687
01:45:31,420 --> 01:45:33,000
Promise?

688
01:45:34,951 --> 01:45:37,421
- Promise?
- Promise, my Osman.

689
01:45:39,216 --> 01:45:40,796
Promise.

690
01:45:47,986 --> 01:45:49,486
Bala...

691
01:46:32,755 --> 01:46:37,545
Do you know why I took you off
commendership, Vladius?

692
01:46:38,955 --> 01:46:41,998
You may think that I should be insulted,
Nicola.

693
01:46:41,998 --> 01:46:46,468
No! Contrarily, I don't think...

694
01:46:46,619 --> 01:46:50,809
that you should be insulted. That's
why I did it in front of everyone's eyes

695
01:46:50,809 --> 01:46:57,455
My dear friend. I wanted everyone to think
that I gave up my hope on you.

696
01:46:57,455 --> 01:47:01,405
Because I am still hopeful, Vladius.

697
01:47:07,518 --> 01:47:12,398
In the mountains, in forests you are
going to live.

698
01:47:12,514 --> 01:47:18,994
You are going to be murderer of
everyone...

699
01:47:19,100 --> 01:47:22,830
whose goes to Kayı Tribe.

700
01:47:26,476 --> 01:47:31,196
Our main objective is that shepherd Osman.

701
01:47:32,041 --> 01:47:35,661
Our second objective is Kayıs.

702
01:47:37,311 --> 01:47:43,501
And the third, Vladius, is the
rest of the Turks.

703
01:47:44,112 --> 01:47:48,179
All of them, Vladius.
All of them.

704
01:47:48,179 --> 01:47:52,868
You are going to kill every one of them!
Are you in, Vladius?

705
01:47:52,868 --> 01:47:57,558
I promise you, Nicola!
Until the end of my life!

706
01:47:58,407 --> 01:47:59,987
Nice.

707
01:48:00,948 --> 01:48:05,278
Nice.
You can go to your duty now.

708
01:48:39,317 --> 01:48:43,992
I promise you Nicola.
None of the Turks will be happy.

709
01:48:43,992 --> 01:48:47,092
Until Osman dies.

710
01:48:47,158 --> 01:48:50,278
Then I will die in peace.

711
01:48:58,421 --> 01:49:01,281
Geyhatu learned what Osman did.

712
01:49:02,515 --> 01:49:06,075
He is preparing a punishment
with his army.

713
01:49:06,380 --> 01:49:10,160
He contacted me for the last warning.

714
01:49:10,804 --> 01:49:16,564
If Osman and Nicola don't make peace,
he is going to kill them.

715
01:49:17,676 --> 01:49:21,246
Is Geyhatu now talking to Osman?

716
01:49:22,983 --> 01:49:28,653
Why does he say "Nicola and Osman" instead
of Inegol Governor and Kayı Bey?

717
01:49:28,653 --> 01:49:31,933
Because this is their war.

718
01:49:32,574 --> 01:49:37,324
It seems we are not a problem for
Geyhatu.

719
01:49:37,908 --> 01:49:44,078
Yavlar Arslan! We trusted you and went to
that dog's place, we nearly died!

720
01:49:44,421 --> 01:49:47,814
You are going to pay for this eventually.

721
01:49:47,814 --> 01:49:51,589
Maybe not today, but someday.

722
01:49:51,589 --> 01:49:55,559
No one is going to go that castle
to make peace.

723
01:49:55,695 --> 01:50:00,455
When we go to that castle again,
we go for a conquer.

724
01:50:05,166 --> 01:50:08,316
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come.

725
01:50:11,841 --> 01:50:14,781
My Bey, it's Nicola.
He wants to come in.

726
01:50:16,494 --> 01:50:18,564
Let him in.

727
01:50:32,931 --> 01:50:36,401
Turkish tent.
I like it.

728
01:50:37,168 --> 01:50:40,028
A nice place to meet.

729
01:50:45,453 --> 01:50:46,593
So?

730
01:50:47,906 --> 01:50:49,306
One.

731
01:50:50,292 --> 01:50:51,582
Two.

732
01:50:52,498 --> 01:50:53,878
Three.

733
01:50:55,638 --> 01:50:57,138
Four.

734
01:50:58,572 --> 01:51:02,515
You were supposed to be five.
Who is missing?

735
01:51:02,515 --> 01:51:05,498
Who, who, who?!
Who is missing?

736
01:51:05,498 --> 01:51:08,278
Hah! It's dark Osman!

737
01:51:11,677 --> 01:51:14,247
Dark Osman is missing.

738
01:51:19,871 --> 01:51:22,740
Why am I not surprised?

739
01:51:22,740 --> 01:51:28,523
If that dog continues talking like that,
I won't care Geyhatu...

740
01:51:28,523 --> 01:51:31,100
and kill him right here!

741
01:51:31,100 --> 01:51:35,930
Nicola! I am trying to fix what you've
done in Kulucahisar.

742
01:51:35,930 --> 01:51:38,973
Can you help me?

743
01:51:38,973 --> 01:51:44,363
Okay good, but it seems to me that
you couldn't convince Osman, again.

744
01:51:44,673 --> 01:51:47,693
Who am I going to make peace with?

745
01:51:48,342 --> 01:51:52,643
Osman Bey has a family issiue.

746
01:51:52,643 --> 01:51:54,813
He'll be late.

747
01:51:54,890 --> 01:51:59,910
Ha?
Did Osman have a family?

748
01:52:04,927 --> 01:52:09,785
Now that we are friends, I want to
learn more about this.

749
01:52:09,785 --> 01:52:16,145
Osman Bey is going to marry
Inal Bey's daughter Targun Hatun.

750
01:52:16,463 --> 01:52:18,903
Tar.. Targun...

751
01:52:19,246 --> 01:52:21,416
Targun Hatun?

752
01:52:24,731 --> 01:52:28,281
That man definitely set his mind on being
Kayı Bey.

753
01:52:28,324 --> 01:52:34,360
Or even maybe Osman wants alliance
with Cuman Turks, hah Savcı Bey?

754
01:52:34,360 --> 01:52:39,660
La hawla wala quwwata illa billahil aliyyil azim.
(There is no power and no strenght except for Allah)

755
01:52:47,368 --> 01:52:50,088
- Have you used it before?
- No, sir.

756
01:52:56,267 --> 01:52:58,695
Do you want me to show you how?

757
01:52:58,695 --> 01:53:00,815
I feel honored.

758
01:53:21,277 --> 01:53:24,787
Only I and Nicola will know that I'm here.

759
01:53:26,392 --> 01:53:29,612
No one else.

760
01:53:35,527 --> 01:53:38,007
And if someone does, he'll die.

761
01:54:29,372 --> 01:54:30,782
Aygül.

762
01:54:31,789 --> 01:54:35,210
What is it, inshallah?
Where are you going?

763
01:54:35,210 --> 01:54:37,640
To war.

764
01:54:38,407 --> 01:54:43,259
- What war is that?
- Osman won't stop till getting Kulucahisar.

765
01:54:43,259 --> 01:54:46,539
And I won't stop until he does.

766
01:54:48,607 --> 01:54:50,727
Aygül!

767
01:54:51,226 --> 01:54:53,366
Aygül!

768
01:55:15,229 --> 01:55:18,069
Let's see how good it is.

769
01:55:43,675 --> 01:55:46,775
Where is she off to again?

770
01:55:47,670 --> 01:55:50,950
I don't care where as long as she leaves.

771
01:55:56,478 --> 01:56:01,438
Come Lena, come.
Let's visit our new bride.

772
01:56:02,377 --> 01:56:06,637
Let's warn her about Bala.

773
01:56:37,565 --> 01:56:41,055
I don't really want to talk about this,
but...

774
01:56:41,319 --> 01:56:45,359
I have a feeling that Osman
won't show up.

775
01:56:47,217 --> 01:56:49,857
Osman will come.

776
01:56:50,912 --> 01:56:53,272
He surely will.

777
01:56:53,586 --> 01:56:56,216
He definitely will.

778
01:56:57,226 --> 01:57:00,636
He can choose not to come,
Yavlak Arslan.

779
01:57:01,348 --> 01:57:04,898
I kept my word.
I came here.

780
01:57:05,543 --> 01:57:08,253
Right, Yavlak Arslan?

781
01:57:09,220 --> 01:57:12,120
Who is going to come
if he doesn't?

782
01:57:13,056 --> 01:57:15,506
Geyhatu will.

783
01:57:16,381 --> 01:57:21,051
What is going to happen then?
No people...

784
01:57:22,348 --> 01:57:25,918
and no tent will be still.

785
01:57:48,885 --> 01:57:52,685
Where are you son?
Where are you?

786
01:57:55,548 --> 01:57:57,838
Osman Bey is coming.

787
01:58:01,120 --> 01:58:05,180
Hay Masha Allah(praise be), my valiant.

788
01:58:05,560 --> 01:58:07,950
Here is the Kayı Bey!

789
01:58:10,122 --> 01:58:12,672
Mashallah(praise be) my daughter.

790
01:58:14,042 --> 01:58:16,132
Mashallah.

791
01:58:17,219 --> 01:58:19,529
Salaimun Aleikum.

792
01:58:22,751 --> 01:58:25,961
Welcome, son.

793
01:58:31,533 --> 01:58:33,503
My Bala.

794
01:58:33,768 --> 01:58:36,548
I will go first.

795
01:58:37,730 --> 01:58:43,210
My valiants that I take with me
want to see me in the front.

796
01:58:43,864 --> 01:58:46,894
You should ride in the back.

797
01:58:57,177 --> 01:59:02,017
Don't worry, my Bey. We are going to fight
together with Bala Hatun

798
01:59:02,017 --> 01:59:04,897
Alps are on their way to the castle.

799
01:59:46,302 --> 01:59:48,272
My Allah!

800
01:59:49,701 --> 01:59:54,091
- Let us be the winners!
- Amin.

801
01:59:54,511 --> 02:00:00,371
- Let us destroy the infidels!
- Amin!

802
02:00:01,240 --> 02:00:08,310
- Let us find our aim!
- Amin.

803
02:00:09,108 --> 02:00:13,540
We are on ou rway to Red Apple.
Let us arrive!

804
02:00:13,540 --> 02:00:15,330
Amin!

805
02:00:16,452 --> 02:00:21,252
A handful Turks here, who are here for
the order the world by your name...

806
02:00:21,375 --> 02:00:27,933
We kneel in front of you...

807
02:00:27,933 --> 02:00:33,393
with the honor they've carried through
their ancestors.

808
02:00:33,838 --> 02:00:41,075
Let us be the winners against
the enemy, my Lord.

809
02:00:41,075 --> 02:00:42,665
Amin.

810
02:01:18,342 --> 02:01:25,512
Even the cruel comes strongly, we won't
be shaken.

811
02:01:27,572 --> 02:01:33,222
We will stand tall like a mountain.

812
02:01:34,645 --> 02:01:41,035
We will shake the ground as we walk, and
shake the sky as we shout.

813
02:01:41,266 --> 02:01:43,316
Because we are the children of...

814
02:01:44,847 --> 02:01:48,167
... Oghuz Khan.

815
02:01:49,466 --> 02:01:56,406
Today, we will take Ulucahisar back and
turn there into an Islamıc city.

816
02:01:57,362 --> 02:02:02,362
We will either return from that castle as
the winners or dead as martyrs.

817
02:02:05,774 --> 02:02:09,024
We will either conquer that castle...

818
02:02:10,625 --> 02:02:12,615
... or ...

819
02:02:14,802 --> 02:02:20,602
... no one from this army will return.

820
02:02:21,194 --> 02:02:28,147
- Allahuekber.
- Allahuekber.

821
02:02:30,438 --> 02:02:33,648
- Can we come in, my Bey?
- Come in, Saltuk Bey.

822
02:02:37,712 --> 02:02:40,794
- My Bey.
- Where is Osman Bey?

823
02:02:40,794 --> 02:02:43,734
- Is there any news?
- No news, my Bey.

824
02:02:47,641 --> 02:02:49,751
What do you mean no news?

825
02:02:50,118 --> 02:02:54,518
- Where is Osman Bey?
- We will find him and inform you, my Bey.

826
02:02:54,518 --> 02:02:58,138
Look everywhere, search everywhere. Go!

827
02:03:09,128 --> 02:03:12,918
Could he have gone to Kulucahisar,
Dündar Bey?

828
02:03:31,051 --> 02:03:35,321
Come on, Osman. Show yourself.

829
02:03:36,100 --> 02:03:38,130
Where are you?

830
02:03:57,010 --> 02:03:59,680
Either a martyr or a ghazi.

831
02:03:59,980 --> 02:04:02,630
Either a martyr or a ghazi.

832
02:04:03,767 --> 02:04:06,927
- May Allah be with you, brother.
- With you too, brother.

833
02:04:12,930 --> 02:04:15,500
- Come on.
- Come on.

834
02:04:32,555 --> 02:04:35,845
- Where are you headed, Osman Bey?
- To Kulucahisar.

835
02:04:35,909 --> 02:04:39,178
Aren't we worth fighting this battle,
too?

836
02:04:39,178 --> 02:04:41,818
You are too, Gence Bey.

837
02:04:42,974 --> 02:04:48,004
Who can stop a brave man who wants to die
as a martyr?

838
02:04:52,111 --> 02:04:54,191
Thank you.

839
02:04:58,812 --> 02:05:00,982
Let's go.

840
02:05:09,937 --> 02:05:15,927
The Turks broke the wall and got inside!
Here! Hurry up! Come on!

841
02:05:16,666 --> 02:05:19,456
Hurry up! Come on!

842
02:05:21,506 --> 02:05:24,737
What is happening?
What is happening here?

843
02:05:27,558 --> 02:05:30,108
From where they are attacking?

844
02:05:30,602 --> 02:05:32,882
Hurry up! Come on!

845
02:05:33,665 --> 02:05:37,345
Hurry up! Here!
Come on!

846
02:05:39,218 --> 02:05:41,427
From where they are attacking?

847
02:05:41,427 --> 02:05:44,907
Run! Run! Come on!

848
02:05:45,808 --> 02:05:48,593
Come on! Hurry up!

849
02:05:48,593 --> 02:05:50,853
What's happening here?

850
02:05:51,732 --> 02:05:54,655
From where they are attacking?
From where?

851
02:05:54,655 --> 02:05:58,210
They broke the wall and got in!

852
02:05:58,210 --> 02:06:00,210
This is impossible.

853
02:06:08,775 --> 02:06:11,235
This is impossible!

854
02:06:11,724 --> 02:06:14,484
Hey, you! Hey!

855
02:06:16,651 --> 02:06:19,371
Come on, Boran. Come on.

856
02:06:19,827 --> 02:06:23,807
Bring that deaf guy to me!

857
02:06:25,690 --> 02:06:28,266
Don't all of you go to the gate!

858
02:06:28,266 --> 02:06:31,376
Find out what happened and inform me!

859
02:06:42,598 --> 02:06:44,548
Come on, come on.

860
02:06:44,965 --> 02:06:47,515
Come on. Come on.

861
02:06:49,011 --> 02:06:49,831
Come on.

862
02:06:54,116 --> 02:06:57,236
Come on.

863
02:07:06,099 --> 02:07:10,379
Wait until we are relieved...

864
02:07:10,945 --> 02:07:13,255
... you pigs.

865
02:07:18,661 --> 02:07:20,221
Ya Allah!

866
02:07:21,684 --> 02:07:27,814
Beys, I came here with good intentions but
I can't say I'm welcomed friendly here.

867
02:07:29,180 --> 02:07:34,400
I am sick of that man's accusations!
Sick of Geyhatu, peace and all of it!

868
02:07:34,400 --> 02:07:37,721
Savcı Bey!
Savcı Bey calm down.

869
02:07:37,721 --> 02:07:41,871
If you want to keep Kulucahisar, you
have to accept our deal. Otherwise..

870
02:07:41,871 --> 02:07:43,409
Or what?

871
02:07:43,847 --> 02:07:48,867
- Will you announce war?
- Don't confuse me with Osman, Nicola.

872
02:07:49,221 --> 02:07:53,347
I won't come with a few alps.
You are talking to the Head Alp!

873
02:07:53,347 --> 02:07:58,227
I can come with all the valiants of
Kayı tribe and destroy you all over.

874
02:08:03,040 --> 02:08:07,280
What does Head Alp mean actually?

875
02:08:07,625 --> 02:08:10,745
Is it something like Corporal?

876
02:08:18,565 --> 02:08:20,835
Stop this!

877
02:08:23,900 --> 02:08:28,460
There's a Turk inside!
There's a Turk inside!

878
02:09:07,566 --> 02:09:09,926
Turks are coming!

879
02:09:11,538 --> 02:09:14,258
Hold the gates!

880
02:09:39,787 --> 02:09:42,344
Göktuğ, now brother! Now!

881
02:09:42,344 --> 02:09:44,594
Hold the gates!

882
02:09:46,368 --> 02:09:49,648
Stop those Turks!

883
02:09:58,609 --> 02:10:02,849
Stop that one!

884
02:10:07,047 --> 02:10:09,997
Shoot him!

885
02:10:25,370 --> 02:10:28,520
Shoot that dog!

886
02:10:48,010 --> 02:10:50,110
Göktuğ!

887
02:10:54,497 --> 02:10:56,577
My brother!

888
02:11:07,920 --> 02:11:12,690
Archers!
Don't let Kayıs pass!

889
02:11:12,824 --> 02:11:15,144
Kill them all!

890
02:11:21,860 --> 02:11:23,730
Die!

891
02:11:41,514 --> 02:11:43,514
Die!

892
02:12:01,608 --> 02:12:06,458
- Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the greatest)
- Damn it!

893
02:12:09,727 --> 02:12:12,317
Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the greatest)

894
02:12:12,555 --> 02:12:15,782
Osman!
Damn it!

895
02:12:15,782 --> 02:12:18,042
Göktuğ! Brother!

896
02:12:18,820 --> 02:12:21,370
Allah-u Akbar! (Allah is the greatest)

897
02:12:26,918 --> 02:12:28,948
Göktuğ!

898
02:12:32,021 --> 02:12:34,291
Damn it!

899
02:12:35,154 --> 02:12:37,127
Osman!

900
02:12:38,127 --> 02:12:47,157
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com